keep-data: the old system Debian GNU/Linux 12 (bookworm) (old.example.net) on /dev/mapper/vg0-root; UEFI firmware; the layout of the profile is not applied, no disk is wiped or partitioned
FORMAT (what is on them is lost)
  /dev/mapper/vg0-root  ext4  /  (10G)
  /dev/vda2             ext4  /boot  (1G)
KEEP (as they are, mounted where they were)
  /dev/vda1             vfat  /boot/efi  (the EFI system partition: not formatted, the new boot loader is added)
  /dev/vda4             ext4  /srv/plain
  /dev/vda4             ext4  /srv/again
  /dev/mapper/vg0-data  xfs   /data
  /dev/mapper/vg0-var   ext4  /srv/var
UNTOUCHED (not in the old fstab: left as they are)
  /dev/mapper/vg0-swap  swap  1G
LOST (on the old root, beyond the system itself)
  /backup  2M
  /etc  6M
  /home/alice  1.1G
  /home/bob  1M
  /opt  245M
  /root  1M
  /usr/local  69M
  /var/lib/apt  176M
  /var/lib/docker  8.5G
WARNINGS
  /dev/dm-1 (/srv/var) is named as the old system's kernel named it; here that is /dev/mapper/vg0-var (ext4, 5G): taken for the volume meant, and named by its UUID from now on
  /dev/disk/by-id/virtio-gone-part9 (/mnt/gone) of the old fstab is dropped: the device is not there
--- /etc/fstab
# /etc/fstab, written by UMP (keep-data: the root made anew, the old system's other volumes as they were)
UUID=NEW-vg0-root  /  ext4  defaults,errors=remount-ro  0 1
UUID=NEW-vda2  /boot  ext4  defaults  0 2
UUID=769B-CE7F  /boot/efi  vfat  umask=0077  0 1
PARTLABEL=plain-part  /srv/plain  ext4  defaults  0 2
/dev/disk/by-label/plain  /srv/again  ext4  noauto  0 0
/dev/disk/by-id/dm-name-vg0-data  /data  xfs  defaults  0 2
UUID=77c86345-9a61-5dbf-9a5d-d648dd9ab76f  /srv/var  ext4  defaults  0 2
